{title: Since I Have Been Redeemed}
{artist: Edwin Excell}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}

Verse 1
I have a [G]song I love to sing, since I have been re[D]deemed,
of my Re[G]deemer, Savior, King — since [D]I have been re[G]deemed.

Chorus
Since [G]I have been re[C]deemed, since [G]I have been re[D]deemed,
I will [G]glory in his [C]name; since [G]I have been re[D]deemed,
I will [G]glory in my [D]Savior's [G]name.
